From 370ddaaabd19e1b2be6844ac79dabda6ff29daa6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 06:56:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/17] test-posix: Check strtok_r, strndup and strcoll_l

strtok and strtok_r: separators that change, the end of the string,
uninitialized state that never points outside the string, interleaved
strings and threads. strdup and strndup: limits, termination and
ENOMEM. strcoll, strxfrm and their _l forms: byte order in the POSIX
locale, agreement with each other, strxfrm's limit and length, and the
locale argument rather than the current one.
---
